{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\ShareAuditDashboard\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ocp-since-above-min",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/Service/OrphanTransferService.php:232 OCP\\Share\\Events\\ShareTransferredEvent: there since Nextcloud 33, the app declares from 31"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 use in 1 file of the public API that the oldest majors of Nextcloud 31 to 35 do not have yet. Either min-version in appinfo/info.xml goes up, or the app does without it there.",
        "  lib/Service/OrphanTransferService.php:232 OCP\\Share\\Events\\ShareTransferredEvent: there since Nextcloud 33, the app declares from 31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "display-name-lookup",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/Service/DisplayNameResolver.php:49",
        "lib/Service/RecipientLookupService.php:444"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "2 places load a user with IUserManager::get() only to ask for the display name. IUserManager::getDisplayName(), there since Nextcloud 25, answers from a cache and loads no user.",
        "  lib/Service/DisplayNameResolver.php:49",
        "  lib/Service/RecipientLookupService.php:444"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boot-listener",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:46 injectFn()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "boot() registers a listener or takes a service from the container in 1 place. boot() runs once for every process of the server, so each of them is built on every request. registerEventListener() in register() builds a listener only when its event fires.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:46 injectFn()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-unreferenced",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "GET /index.php/apps/share_audit_dashboard/  share_audit_dashboard.page.index  appinfo/routes.php:18 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 1 route outside OCS. Looked for: a route name or a path in the PHP source and the templates, in 29 files of the frontend source and in the navigation of info.xml. The frontend puts the path of the app and the rest of a URL together at run time, so every text there that reads like a path below the app counted as a call. A route stays behind when the frontend stops calling it. A route that only a client outside the app calls shows here as well, unless its method allows requests from other origins (CORS).",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/share_audit_dashboard/  share_audit_dashboard.page.index  appinfo/routes.php:18 routes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "phpunit/phpunit is in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
